# MnemoNotes

Pharmacy-first scheduling and operations notes (shifts, personnel, reminders, acknowledgements). Keep the scheduling model generic enough for other shift-based businesses later.

## Stack

- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript
- Supabase (Auth, Postgres, RLS, Realtime, Edge Functions)
- FullCalendar, TanStack Query, React Router, RHF + Zod
- Plain CSS (no Tailwind). Vitest + Testing Library. Package manager: pnpm

## Roles

`developer_admin` | `owner` | `manager` | `personnel` | `viewer`

Permission source of truth: `src/lib/access-control.ts` and Supabase `role_permissions` / RLS. Keep frontend checks aligned with backend policies.

## Architecture

- Feature folders under `src/features/*`; shared UI in `src/components`
- Calendar-first shell: top app bar; extra UI in modals/popups (`Modal`)
- Demo data is OK until Supabase is wired; prefer live paths via Edge Functions for owner registration and personnel invites (service-role / trusted server work)
- Never expose service-role keys in the browser; never commit secrets
- Platform admin hard-deletes and auth status changes go through `supabase/functions/admin-records`

## When implementing

Prefer extending existing screens/patterns over new frameworks or UI kits. After schema changes: `pnpm supabase:types`.
